title: "collator-protocol: V4 segment handling on the experimental validator side"
doc:
- audience: Node Dev
  description: |-
    This PR implements V4 segment advertisements in `validator_side_experimental`. The
    legacy validator side does not support V4. V1-V3 handling is unchanged.

    - A stored segment is one fetch entitlement, spent when a fetch launches. At fetch
      time the entries are walked oldest-first and the first output head that is not
      fetched, not in flight and not known to prospective-parachains is requested.
      Re-advertised blocks are deduplicated by output head.
    - A segment whose entries are all known to prospective-parachains is dropped
      without a fetch. One blocked only by fetched or in-flight heads is held and
      retried when the pending attempt concludes.
    - Segments with a zero-length cycle (parent head == output head) are rejected.
      Byte-identical segments from the same peer are rejected while stored; a
      re-advertisement after the fetch launched is a new entitlement.
    - The planner pass runs only after a change that can enable a launch (view update,
      accepted advertisement, concluded fetch, released slot, fetch timer) instead of
      after every message.
    - Adds `ProspectiveParachainsMessage::GetKnownOutputHeads`: per scheduling parent
      still in view and para, the output heads of all held candidates plus the para's
      latest included head. The validator side queries it before each planner pass.
      Knowledge under a sibling relay fork does not block a fetch.
crates:
- name: polkadot-collator-protocol
  bump: minor
  validate: false
- name: polkadot-node-core-prospective-parachains
  bump: minor
  validate: false
- name: polkadot-node-subsystem-types
  bump: major
  validate: false
